<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 2nd century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 100s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/2nd-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 150 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10711 5638" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 150 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="5304" cy="942" r="182"/><text x="5304" y="1018" font-size="219">1</text></g><g><circle cx="6757" cy="1168" r="182"/><text x="6757" y="1245" font-size="219">2</text></g><g><circle cx="7769" cy="1191" r="182"/><text x="7769" y="1267" font-size="219">3</text></g><g><circle cx="5772" cy="1297" r="182"/><text x="5772" y="1373" font-size="219">4</text></g><g><circle cx="2331" cy="1704" r="182"/><text x="2331" y="1781" font-size="219">5</text></g><g><circle cx="7165" cy="1820" r="182"/><text x="7165" y="1896" font-size="219">6</text></g><g><circle cx="6060" cy="1908" r="182"/><text x="6060" y="1984" font-size="219">7</text></g><g><circle cx="6152" cy="991" r="182"/><text x="6152" y="1067" font-size="219">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 150 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Caucasian Albania &middot; Roman Empire &middot; Satavahana dynasty &middot; Teotihuacan &middot; Kushan Empire &middot; Aksumite Empire &middot; Han Dynasty &middot; Roman Egypt</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 3 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Yellow Turban Rebellion</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Trajan's Dacian Wars</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Marcomannic Wars</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Septimius Severus</li><li>Cao Cao</li><li>Marcus Aurelius</li><li>Tertullian</li><li>Claudius Ptolemy</li><li>Galen</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>145–211 CE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 155 – c. 220</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>155–220 CE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>121–180</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>129–c. 216 CE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 100–c. 170 CE</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">These words appear in the entries of this century. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Arabic language</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Latin</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Nasi (title)</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 100s, 49 recorded states were founded and 16 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Roman Empire, the Kushan Empire and the Han Dynasty. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 2nd century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/2nd-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 2nd century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Roman Empire <span>27 BCE – 476 CE</span></li><li>Kushan Empire <span>30 CE – 375 CE</span></li><li>Han Dynasty <span>206 BCE – 220 CE</span></li><li>Roman Egypt <span>30 BCE – 641 CE</span></li><li>Teotihuacan <span>100 BCE – 550 CE</span></li><li>Satavahana dynasty <span>100 BCE – 220 CE</span></li><li>Aksumite Empire <span>100 CE – 940 CE</span></li><li>Caucasian Albania <span>100 BCE – 510 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Trajan's Dacian Wars <span>101–102 CE; 105–106 CE</span></li><li>Marcomannic Wars <span>166–180</span></li><li>Yellow Turban Rebellion <span>184 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Septimius Severus <span>1: 145–211 CE</span></li><li>Cao Cao <span>3: 155–220 CE</span></li><li>Marcus Aurelius <span>4: 121–180</span></li><li>Tertullian <span>2: c. 155 – c. 220</span></li><li>Claudius Ptolemy <span>6: c. 100–c. 170 CE</span></li><li>Galen <span>5: 129–c. 216 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Arabic language</dt><dd>Arabic is a Semitic language that spread with Islam from the Arabian Peninsula across the Middle East and North Africa.</dd><dt>Latin</dt><dd>Latin is the language of ancient Rome, which spread across the western Mediterranean with Roman rule and became the root of the Romance languages.</dd><dt>Nasi (title)</dt><dd>Nasi is a Hebrew title meaning 'prince' or 'leader', used in the Hebrew Bible for tribal chiefs.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
